<title>GERMANY: Bilfinger wins 300 mln dmk Thai motorway contract.</title>
<headline>Bilfinger wins 300 mln dmk Thai motorway contract.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Bilfinger + Berger AG said on Monday it had won a share worth 300 million marks in a contract to build a motorway in Bangkok.</p>
<p>In a statement, the group said the contract was to build a 32-kilometre stretch of motorway and other supporting structures, planned for completion by the end of 1999. Work will begin in December.</p>
<p>The contract was awarded by the Northern Bangkok Expressway Company. Bilfinger will share the contract, worth 600 million marks, with its Thai partner, Chor Karnchang PCL.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
